1. Component Creation
Create all components as React components in the src\business-apps folder.
All folders in src\business-apps folder are products that we have, e.g. crm, irm.
All folders in src\business-apps\(crm|irm) are either named `detail-screens` or `overview-screens` or `flow-screens`.
All folders in src\business-apps\(crm|irm)\(detail-screens|overview-screensflow-screens) are names of screens, e.g. LeadDetail.
All files in src\business-apps\(crm|irm)\(detail-screens|overview-screensflow-screens)\<screenName> are files related to that screen.
Example of correctly create components:
- src\business-apps\irm\detail-screens\LeadDetail\LeadDetail.tsx
- src\business-apps\irm\overview-screens\LeadOverview\LeadOverview.tsx
- src\business-apps\crm\overview-screens\OpportunityOverview\OpportunityOverview.tsx
The place where components are exported is: src\business-apps\index.ts
The place where the exported components are imported into the local development preview is: src\index.map.ts
Always add a new components in both src\business-apps\index.ts and src\index.map.ts.

2. Component Development
Use ant-design for React UI components
Use typescript for type safety
Use prettier for code styling
User eslint for linting
